trait-claustrophobia-name = Claustrophobia
trait-claustrophobia-desc = You are terrified of small spaces. If you are placed inside any locker, crate, or container, a severe panic attack sets in and you struggle to breathe.

claustrophobia-panic = You feel trapped! Must escape... can't breathe...
claustrophobia-panic-stage-1 = The walls feel suffocatingly close... the air feels heavy and tight.
claustrophobia-panic-stage-2 = You struggle to breathe! Your chest tightens and your heart races in panic!
claustrophobia-panic-stage-3 = YOU CAN'T BREATHE!! TERROR OVERWHELMS YOU, MUST GET OUT NOW!!
claustrophobia-relief = You inhale fresh, open air as your lungs finally calm down...

claustrophobia-record-text = Patient demonstrates severe claustrophobia, experiencing acute hyperventilation and panic inside enclosed containers.
claustrophobia-scan-warning = [!] SCAN ALERT: Acute claustrophobia with panic-induced hyperventilation in enclosed spaces.
